# Two gas buffers that earn nothing, filling quietly and emptying hard.
#
# This is `03-compact` with a tank in each steam line, and it makes exactly the
# same 108 MW on the same water for two more vessels and eight more tiles. The
# buffers are genuinely working -- the inspector will show them cycling between
# 200 and 1600 -- and it changes nothing, because a turbine's intake port is
# already a buffer and the tank is only ever filling in what the port would
# have held anyway.
#
# It is here because experiment 07 ended by saying exactly that about the whole
# store family, and because experiment 08 gives the sentence a picture: two
# tall vessels in the middle of a plant, doing nothing, in a silhouette you can
# recognise from the far end of the yard.

machine "Buffered"
brief power

reactor   R1  at 0,0   throttle 40

exchanger HX1 at 5,0
exchanger HX2 at 5,4

tank      TK1 at 9,0   pulse 1600 200
tank      TK2 at 9,4   pulse 1600 200

turbine   T1  at 13,0
turbine   T2  at 13,4

generator G1  at 17,0
generator G2  at 17,4

pump      W1  at 0,5

wire R1.heat -> HX1.heat
wire R1.heat -> HX2.heat
wire W1.water -> HX1.water
wire W1.water -> HX2.water

wire HX1.steam -> TK1.in
wire HX2.steam -> TK2.in
wire TK1.out -> T1.steam
wire TK2.out -> T2.steam

wire T1.rotary -> G1.rotary
wire T2.rotary -> G2.rotary
